        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ci): stabilize dead-export analysis",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe unused-export ratchet could change after `pnpm build` because Knip still analyzed generated root `dist/**` output. The same ratchet also retained four test-only OpenAI transport helpers as named production-facade exports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRoot `dist/**` is excluded through both Knip mechanisms required by the pinned 6.8.0 contract: `ignoreFiles` for unused-file findings and `ignore` for every issue type. The existing ratchet test pins both settings.\n\n`buildOpenAIResponsesParams`, `parseTransportChunkUsage`, and `resolveAzureOpenAIApiVersion` remain private to their implementation modules and are available to repository tests only through the existing `testing` facade. The redundant sanitizer facade export and duplicate sanitizer test are removed; the canonical implementation and coverage remain in `transport-stream-shared`.\n\nTransport constructors and the explicitly SDK-exported `buildOpenAICompletionsParams` remain unchanged. The merge drops the four facade rows, and the LOC v2 baseline records the source reductions. The older merge-base diff also shows four sidebar baseline deletions already present on current `main`; they are a no-op at merge.\n\nThe root `dist/**` stabilization was identified in https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/105945. That branch is uneditable and overlaps current `main` plus this cleanup, so its unique two-file fix is preserved here with Peter Steinberger as commit author.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior changes. Dead-export enforcement is deterministic before and after builds, and the internal OpenAI transport surface is smaller.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `corepack pnpm test:serial test/scripts/check-deadcode-exports.test.ts src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts src/agents/schema-normalization-runtime-contract.test.ts` - 342 tests passed\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs` before and after `corepack pnpm build` - identical 5,498-entry baseline\n- `corepack pnpm check:changed -- <10 changed paths>` - passed across core, core tests, root tests, and tooling lanes\n- Production LOC drops: completions transport 1,948 to 1,946; Responses transport 2,602 to 2,601\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcv5gfs47jj2akj67nt7w0w`\n- Fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` medium branch autoreview - no findings, 0.97 confidence\n",
        "branch": "fix/ts-loc-ratchet-drift",
